Derived files, and their upstream origin:

  ink_tokenizer/codec.py
      `text_to_tokens` and `detokenize` ported from `colab.ipynb`.
      `tokenize` / `tokens_to_text` are original to this project.

  ink_tokenizer/preprocess.py
      `scale_and_pad` and the inverse mapping follow `scale_and_pad` and
      `unpad_unscale_unrotate_uncrop` from `colab.ipynb`.

  services/inksight/tf_compat.py
      Ported from `utils/tensorflow.py`.

The InkSight-Small-p model weights (Derendering/InkSight-Small-p on the
Hugging Face Hub) are separately licensed under Apache 2.0 and are not
redistributed here; they are downloaded at runtime.

Upstream asks that the model not be used for forging handwriting or for
privacy-intruding applications.

The fixed-vocabulary digital-ink representation in ``ink_tokenizer/scribe.py``
is an independent implementation based on the ScribeTokens method described
by Douglass Wang, "ScribeTokens: Fixed-Vocabulary Tokenization of Digital Ink"
(arXiv:2603.02805) and its accompanying repository:

    https://github.com/douglasswng/scribe-tokens

It is kept distinct from the InkSight token wire format and contains no source
code copied from that repository.
